{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Charts builds a platform-neutral scene before the selected renderer\nproduces output. React, Preact, Vue, Solid, Svelte, Angular, and Octane use the same\nruntime and renderer on the server and in the browser."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"adapter-support","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adapter support"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adapter"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server output"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Browser contract"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../framework/react/adapter.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SVG, Canvas, or mixed shell"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hydrates and adopts the existing surface"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../framework/preact/adapter.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Preact"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SVG or mixed shell"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hydrates before the shared host mounts"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../framework/vue/adapter.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vue"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SVG or mixed shell"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hydrates before the shared host mounts"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../framework/solid/adapter.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solid"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SVG or mixed shell"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hydrates before the shared host mounts"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../framework/svelte/adapter.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Svelte"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SVG or mixed shell"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hydrates before the shared host mounts"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../framework/octane/adapter.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Octane"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SVG, Canvas, or mixed shell"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hydrates and adopts the existing surface"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../framework/angular/adapter.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Angular"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SVG"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hydrates and adopts the existing surface"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../framework/lit/adapter.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lit"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Not yet a verified adapter contract"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Browser registration, update, disconnect, reconnect"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../framework/alpine/adapter.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Alpine"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Browser-only directive"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For adapters with server output, the browser must render the same definition,\ndimensions, formatters, and component tree. Angular uses\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"provideClientHydration"},{"type":"text","value":"; see its adapter page for the verified version scope.\nLit may run inside applications with their own server infrastructure, but this\nlibrary does not yet promise or test adapter hydration for Lit."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"give-the-server-a-real-size","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Give the server a real size"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The server cannot measure a container. Supply one of these policies:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height"},{"type":"text","value":" for a fixed-size chart;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aspectRatio"},{"type":"text","value":" for a fixed-width proportional chart;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialWidth"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height"},{"type":"text","value":" for a responsive chart;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialWidth"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aspectRatio"},{"type":"text","value":" when height should follow width."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When CSS owns height and neither height option is present, server output uses\nthe "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"320"},{"type":"text","value":" fallback. The browser adopts the positive measured container content\nheight after mounting. Supply "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height"},{"type":"text","value":" when exact server height matters."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<Chart\n  definition={trafficChart}\n  ariaLabel=\"Daily traffic\"\n  initialWidth={720}\n  aspectRatio={16 / 9}\n/>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The adapter uses an explicit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width"},{"type":"text","value":" before "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialWidth"},{"type":"text","value":" when deriving the\nserver height. After mounting, a responsive host observes the container and\nrenders at its measured content width and any CSS-owned height. Pick an\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialWidth"},{"type":"text","value":" close to the layout's common size to minimize the first\nresponsive adjustment."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"./responsive-charts.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Responsive Charts"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the complete size policy."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"keep-output-deterministic","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep output deterministic"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server and first-client output must agree for the same definition, size, and\noptions. In particular:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"keep fixed definitions at module scope and recreate captured-data definitions\nfrom the same resolved data;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"sort unordered collections before creating marks;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"do not read "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"window"},{"type":"text","value":", layout, time, locale, or random values while building a\ndefinition;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"pass locale-sensitive formatters explicitly;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"rely on inferred IDs or unique positions, and supply explicit keys when the\ndata has no stable identity;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"provide "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"idPrefix"},{"type":"text","value":" when multiple render roots need coordinated resource IDs."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Responsive chart functions are synchronous. Fetch and transform data in the\napplication's server/data layer, then capture the resolved data in the\ndefinition."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"hydration-ownership","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hydration ownership"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server and browser executions create separate runtime instances. Within the\nbrowser adapter's own initial render and layout-effect mount, the DOM host\nreceives the already created browser runtime."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Do not conditionally replace a chart with a different component only because\nthe code is executing on the server. That creates a different tree and gives\nup the shared render path."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"client-only-react-charts","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client-only React charts"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To skip chart compilation and SVG output on the server, let the application\nmount the chart after hydration. Reserve its space with an ordinary wrapper:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"'use client'\n\nimport { useEffect, useState, type ReactNode } from 'react'\n\nexport function ClientOnlyChart({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) {\n  const [mounted, setMounted] = useState(false)\n  useEffect(() => setMounted(true), [])\n\n  return (\n    <div style={{ width: '100%', height: 260 }}>\n      {mounted ? children : null}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wrap a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<Chart height={260} ... />"},{"type":"text","value":" in this component. The server and first\nbrowser render both contain the empty wrapper, then the effect mounts the\nchart. Match the wrapper height to the chart, or give both the same aspect\nratio. The wrapper is application-owned, there is no "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prerender"},{"type":"text","value":" prop on\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Chart"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This skips the child's rendering, not work done by its parent to prepare data\nor construct definitions. Put browser-only setup inside the mounted child.\nIn Next.js, keep this wrapper and chart definitions within a client component\nas described in the "},{"type":"link","href":"../framework/react/adapter.md#nextjs-app-router","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Do not switch based on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"typeof window"},{"type":"text","value":" during render, the server and first\nbrowser trees would differ. This pattern also gives up visible chart geometry\nbefore JavaScript loads, so keep normal SVG SSR when that matters."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"canvas-server-shell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Canvas server shell"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/react/canvas"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/octane/canvas"},{"type":"text","value":" render a\ndeterministic accessible shell on the server: a named chart root and five\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aria-hidden"},{"type":"text","value":" canvas elements with the initial scene dimensions. The hidden\nstable base bitmap preserves the raw "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"canvas"},{"type":"text","value":" surface, while four live layers\nmodel background, focus underlay, ordinary scene, and focus overlay paint. No\nserver Canvas API or pixel painting is required."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The client renders the same shell, adopts its existing root and canvases, sizes\ntheir backing stores for the device-pixel ratio, paints the scene, and attaches\nthe shared interaction host. The first image appears after client mount; use\nthe default SVG adapter when visible server-rendered geometry is required."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When selected marks use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"canvasChartRenderer"},{"type":"text","value":", verified server adapters emit\none accessible mixed root with ordered SVG markup and Canvas shells. The\nbrowser adopts each child surface. SVG marks remain visible in the server\nresponse, while Canvas marks receive pixels after mount."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"fonts-and-text-measurement","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fonts and text measurement"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Automatic guide margins depend on text metrics. The server uses deterministic\nfallback measurement unless you provide "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"measureText"},{"type":"text","value":". The browser host\nremeasures when fonts become available and schedules a new layout."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartTextMeasurer"},{"type":"text","value":" is deliberately synchronous. Its options include the\nresolved family, style, stretch, letter spacing, direction, locale, and font\nscale so server and native implementations can use the same typography\ncontract. Hosts own asynchronous font readiness and request another render\nafter their available metrics change."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For strict pixel parity:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use a font available in both environments."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Supply a deterministic "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartTextMeasurer"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Supply the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartTextTypography"},{"type":"text","value":", including locale and font scale, in\nboth environments."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Most applications should allow the browser's post-font layout correction\ninstead of shipping a font engine to the server."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"render-without-a-framework","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Render without a framework"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createChartRuntime"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderChartSvg"},{"type":"text","value":" form the server boundary:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createChartRuntime, renderChartSvg } from '@tanstack/charts'\n\nconst runtime = createChartRuntime<TrafficRow, Date, number>()\nconst scene = runtime.render(definition, { width: 720, height: 400 })\n\nconst svg = renderChartSvg(scene, {\n  ariaLabel: 'Daily traffic',\n  idPrefix: 'traffic',\n})\n\nruntime.destroy()","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderChartSvg"},{"type":"text","value":" returns a string and does not require a DOM. A custom\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartRenderer.prerender"},{"type":"text","value":" may produce another deterministic shell. Browser-only\nfocus, tooltip, reconciliation or paint, animation, and export begin when its\nsurface mounts."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"hydration-checklist","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hydration checklist"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server data is fully resolved before chart rendering."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Initial dimensions are explicit and representative."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Definition, transformed data, and formatting are deterministic."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keys and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"idPrefix"},{"type":"text","value":" are stable."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The same adapter and definition render on both sides."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Browser-only work lives in host callbacks or application effects."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Font-driven relayout is expected or a text measurer is supplied."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the selected framework adapter page and\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../reference/runtime-and-scene.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Runtime and Scene"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the exact contracts."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"adapter-support","text":"Adapter support","level":2},{"id":"give-the-server-a-real-size","text":"Give the server a real size","level":2},{"id":"keep-output-deterministic","text":"Keep output deterministic","level":2},{"id":"hydration-ownership","text":"Hydration ownership","level":2},{"id":"client-only-react-charts","text":"Client-only React charts","level":2},{"id":"canvas-server-shell","text":"Canvas server shell","level":2},{"id":"fonts-and-text-measurement","text":"Fonts and text measurement","level":2},{"id":"render-without-a-framework","text":"Render without a framework","level":2},{"id":"hydration-checklist","text":"Hydration checklist","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack Charts builds a platform-neutral scene before the selected renderer\nproduces output. React, Preact, Vue, Solid, Svelte, Angular, and Octane use the same\nruntime and renderer on the server and in the browser.\n\n## Adapter support\n\n| Adapter                                    | Server output                       | Browser contract                                    |\n| ------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| [React](../framework/react/adapter.md)     | SVG, Canvas, or mixed shell         | Hydrates and adopts the existing surface            |\n| [Preact](../framework/preact/adapter.md)   | SVG or mixed shell                  | Hydrates before the shared host mounts              |\n| [Vue](../framework/vue/adapter.md)         | SVG or mixed shell                  | Hydrates before the shared host mounts              |\n| [Solid](../framework/solid/adapter.md)     | SVG or mixed shell                  | Hydrates before the shared host mounts              |\n| [Svelte](../framework/svelte/adapter.md)   | SVG or mixed shell                  | Hydrates before the shared host mounts              |\n| [Octane](../framework/octane/adapter.md)   | SVG, Canvas, or mixed shell         | Hydrates and adopts the existing surface            |\n| [Angular](../framework/angular/adapter.md) | SVG                                 | Hydrates and adopts the existing surface            |\n| [Lit](../framework/lit/adapter.md)         | Not yet a verified adapter contract | Browser registration, update, disconnect, reconnect |\n| [Alpine](../framework/alpine/adapter.md)   | None                                | Browser-only directive                              |\n\nFor adapters with server output, the browser must render the same definition,\ndimensions, formatters, and component tree. Angular uses\n`provideClientHydration`; see its adapter page for the verified version scope.\nLit may run inside applications with their own server infrastructure, but this\nlibrary does not yet promise or test adapter hydration for Lit.\n\n## Give the server a real size\n\nThe server cannot measure a container. Supply one of these policies:\n\n- `width` and `height` for a fixed-size chart;\n- `width` and `aspectRatio` for a fixed-width proportional chart;\n- `initialWidth` and `height` for a responsive chart;\n- `initialWidth` and `aspectRatio` when height should follow width.\n\nWhen CSS owns height and neither height option is present, server output uses\nthe `320` fallback. The browser adopts the positive measured container content\nheight after mounting. Supply `height` when exact server height matters.\n\n```tsx\n<Chart\n  definition={trafficChart}\n  ariaLabel=\"Daily traffic\"\n  initialWidth={720}\n  aspectRatio={16 / 9}\n/>\n```\n\nThe adapter uses an explicit `width` before `initialWidth` when deriving the\nserver height. After mounting, a responsive host observes the container and\nrenders at its measured content width and any CSS-owned height. Pick an\n`initialWidth` close to the layout's common size to minimize the first\nresponsive adjustment.\n\nSee [Responsive Charts](./responsive-charts.md) for the complete size policy.\n\n## Keep output deterministic\n\nServer and first-client output must agree for the same definition, size, and\noptions. In particular:\n\n- keep fixed definitions at module scope and recreate captured-data definitions\n  from the same resolved data;\n- sort unordered collections before creating marks;\n- do not read `window`, layout, time, locale, or random values while building a\n  definition;\n- pass locale-sensitive formatters explicitly;\n- rely on inferred IDs or unique positions, and supply explicit keys when the\n  data has no stable identity;\n- provide `idPrefix` when multiple render roots need coordinated resource IDs.\n\nResponsive chart functions are synchronous. Fetch and transform data in the\napplication's server/data layer, then capture the resolved data in the\ndefinition.\n\n## Hydration ownership\n\nServer and browser executions create separate runtime instances. Within the\nbrowser adapter's own initial render and layout-effect mount, the DOM host\nreceives the already created browser runtime.\n\nDo not conditionally replace a chart with a different component only because\nthe code is executing on the server. That creates a different tree and gives\nup the shared render path.\n\n## Client-only React charts\n\nTo skip chart compilation and SVG output on the server, let the application\nmount the chart after hydration. Reserve its space with an ordinary wrapper:\n\n```tsx\n'use client'\n\nimport { useEffect, useState, type ReactNode } from 'react'\n\nexport function ClientOnlyChart({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) {\n  const [mounted, setMounted] = useState(false)\n  useEffect(() => setMounted(true), [])\n\n  return (\n    <div style={{ width: '100%', height: 260 }}>\n      {mounted ? children : null}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nWrap a `<Chart height={260} ... />` in this component. The server and first\nbrowser render both contain the empty wrapper, then the effect mounts the\nchart. Match the wrapper height to the chart, or give both the same aspect\nratio. The wrapper is application-owned, there is no `prerender` prop on\n`Chart`.\n\nThis skips the child's rendering, not work done by its parent to prepare data\nor construct definitions. Put browser-only setup inside the mounted child.\nIn Next.js, keep this wrapper and chart definitions within a client component\nas described in the [React adapter](../framework/react/adapter.md#nextjs-app-router).\n\nDo not switch based on `typeof window` during render, the server and first\nbrowser trees would differ. This pattern also gives up visible chart geometry\nbefore JavaScript loads, so keep normal SVG SSR when that matters.\n\n## Canvas server shell\n\n`@tanstack/charts/react/canvas` and `@tanstack/charts/octane/canvas` render a\ndeterministic accessible shell on the server: a named chart root and five\n`aria-hidden` canvas elements with the initial scene dimensions. The hidden\nstable base bitmap preserves the raw `canvas` surface, while four live layers\nmodel background, focus underlay, ordinary scene, and focus overlay paint. No\nserver Canvas API or pixel painting is required.\n\nThe client renders the same shell, adopts its existing root and canvases, sizes\ntheir backing stores for the device-pixel ratio, paints the scene, and attaches\nthe shared interaction host. The first image appears after client mount; use\nthe default SVG adapter when visible server-rendered geometry is required.\n\nWhen selected marks use `canvasChartRenderer`, verified server adapters emit\none accessible mixed root with ordered SVG markup and Canvas shells. The\nbrowser adopts each child surface. SVG marks remain visible in the server\nresponse, while Canvas marks receive pixels after mount.\n\n## Fonts and text measurement\n\nAutomatic guide margins depend on text metrics. The server uses deterministic\nfallback measurement unless you provide `measureText`. The browser host\nremeasures when fonts become available and schedules a new layout.\n\n`ChartTextMeasurer` is deliberately synchronous. Its options include the\nresolved family, style, stretch, letter spacing, direction, locale, and font\nscale so server and native implementations can use the same typography\ncontract. Hosts own asynchronous font readiness and request another render\nafter their available metrics change.\n\nFor strict pixel parity:\n\n1. Use a font available in both environments.\n2. Supply a deterministic `ChartTextMeasurer`.\n3. Supply the same `ChartTextTypography`, including locale and font scale, in\n   both environments.\n\nMost applications should allow the browser's post-font layout correction\ninstead of shipping a font engine to the server.\n\n## Render without a framework\n\n`createChartRuntime` and `renderChartSvg` form the server boundary:\n\n```ts\nimport { createChartRuntime, renderChartSvg } from '@tanstack/charts'\n\nconst runtime = createChartRuntime<TrafficRow, Date, number>()\nconst scene = runtime.render(definition, { width: 720, height: 400 })\n\nconst svg = renderChartSvg(scene, {\n  ariaLabel: 'Daily traffic',\n  idPrefix: 'traffic',\n})\n\nruntime.destroy()\n```\n\n`renderChartSvg` returns a string and does not require a DOM. A custom\n`ChartRenderer.prerender` may produce another deterministic shell. Browser-only\nfocus, tooltip, reconciliation or paint, animation, and export begin when its\nsurface mounts.\n\n## Hydration checklist\n\n- Server data is fully resolved before chart rendering.\n- Initial dimensions are explicit and representative.\n- Definition, transformed data, and formatting are deterministic.\n- Keys and `idPrefix` are stable.\n- The same adapter and definition render on both sides.\n- Browser-only work lives in host callbacks or application effects.\n- Font-driven relayout is expected or a text measurer is supplied.\n\nSee the selected framework adapter page and\n[Runtime and Scene](../reference/runtime-and-scene.md) for the exact contracts.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: SSR and Hydration\ndescription: Render deterministic chart markup on the server, preserve runtime work through hydration, and handle responsive dimensions without mismatches.\n---\n\nTanStack Charts builds a platform-neutral scene before the selected renderer\nproduces output. React, Preact, Vue, Solid, Svelte, Angular, and Octane use the same\nruntime and renderer on the server and in the browser.\n\n## Adapter support\n\n| Adapter                                    | Server output                       | Browser contract                                    |\n| ------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| [React](../framework/react/adapter.md)     | SVG, Canvas, or mixed shell         | Hydrates and adopts the existing surface            |\n| [Preact](../framework/preact/adapter.md)   | SVG or mixed shell                  | Hydrates before the shared host mounts              |\n| [Vue](../framework/vue/adapter.md)         | SVG or mixed shell                  | Hydrates before the shared host mounts              |\n| [Solid](../framework/solid/adapter.md)     | SVG or mixed shell                  | Hydrates before the shared host mounts              |\n| [Svelte](../framework/svelte/adapter.md)   | SVG or mixed shell                  | Hydrates before the shared host mounts              |\n| [Octane](../framework/octane/adapter.md)   | SVG, Canvas, or mixed shell         | Hydrates and adopts the existing surface            |\n| [Angular](../framework/angular/adapter.md) | SVG                                 | Hydrates and adopts the existing surface            |\n| [Lit](../framework/lit/adapter.md)         | Not yet a verified adapter contract | Browser registration, update, disconnect, reconnect |\n| [Alpine](../framework/alpine/adapter.md)   | None                                | Browser-only directive                              |\n\nFor adapters with server output, the browser must render the same definition,\ndimensions, formatters, and component tree. Angular uses\n`provideClientHydration`; see its adapter page for the verified version scope.\nLit may run inside applications with their own server infrastructure, but this\nlibrary does not yet promise or test adapter hydration for Lit.\n\n## Give the server a real size\n\nThe server cannot measure a container. Supply one of these policies:\n\n- `width` and `height` for a fixed-size chart;\n- `width` and `aspectRatio` for a fixed-width proportional chart;\n- `initialWidth` and `height` for a responsive chart;\n- `initialWidth` and `aspectRatio` when height should follow width.\n\nWhen CSS owns height and neither height option is present, server output uses\nthe `320` fallback. The browser adopts the positive measured container content\nheight after mounting. Supply `height` when exact server height matters.\n\n```tsx\n<Chart\n  definition={trafficChart}\n  ariaLabel=\"Daily traffic\"\n  initialWidth={720}\n  aspectRatio={16 / 9}\n/>\n```\n\nThe adapter uses an explicit `width` before `initialWidth` when deriving the\nserver height. After mounting, a responsive host observes the container and\nrenders at its measured content width and any CSS-owned height. Pick an\n`initialWidth` close to the layout's common size to minimize the first\nresponsive adjustment.\n\nSee [Responsive Charts](./responsive-charts.md) for the complete size policy.\n\n## Keep output deterministic\n\nServer and first-client output must agree for the same definition, size, and\noptions. In particular:\n\n- keep fixed definitions at module scope and recreate captured-data definitions\n  from the same resolved data;\n- sort unordered collections before creating marks;\n- do not read `window`, layout, time, locale, or random values while building a\n  definition;\n- pass locale-sensitive formatters explicitly;\n- rely on inferred IDs or unique positions, and supply explicit keys when the\n  data has no stable identity;\n- provide `idPrefix` when multiple render roots need coordinated resource IDs.\n\nResponsive chart functions are synchronous. Fetch and transform data in the\napplication's server/data layer, then capture the resolved data in the\ndefinition.\n\n## Hydration ownership\n\nServer and browser executions create separate runtime instances. Within the\nbrowser adapter's own initial render and layout-effect mount, the DOM host\nreceives the already created browser runtime.\n\nDo not conditionally replace a chart with a different component only because\nthe code is executing on the server. That creates a different tree and gives\nup the shared render path.\n\n## Client-only React charts\n\nTo skip chart compilation and SVG output on the server, let the application\nmount the chart after hydration. Reserve its space with an ordinary wrapper:\n\n```tsx\n'use client'\n\nimport { useEffect, useState, type ReactNode } from 'react'\n\nexport function ClientOnlyChart({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) {\n  const [mounted, setMounted] = useState(false)\n  useEffect(() => setMounted(true), [])\n\n  return (\n    <div style={{ width: '100%', height: 260 }}>\n      {mounted ? children : null}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nWrap a `<Chart height={260} ... />` in this component. The server and first\nbrowser render both contain the empty wrapper, then the effect mounts the\nchart. Match the wrapper height to the chart, or give both the same aspect\nratio. The wrapper is application-owned, there is no `prerender` prop on\n`Chart`.\n\nThis skips the child's rendering, not work done by its parent to prepare data\nor construct definitions. Put browser-only setup inside the mounted child.\nIn Next.js, keep this wrapper and chart definitions within a client component\nas described in the [React adapter](../framework/react/adapter.md#nextjs-app-router).\n\nDo not switch based on `typeof window` during render, the server and first\nbrowser trees would differ. This pattern also gives up visible chart geometry\nbefore JavaScript loads, so keep normal SVG SSR when that matters.\n\n## Canvas server shell\n\n`@tanstack/charts/react/canvas` and `@tanstack/charts/octane/canvas` render a\ndeterministic accessible shell on the server: a named chart root and five\n`aria-hidden` canvas elements with the initial scene dimensions. The hidden\nstable base bitmap preserves the raw `canvas` surface, while four live layers\nmodel background, focus underlay, ordinary scene, and focus overlay paint. No\nserver Canvas API or pixel painting is required.\n\nThe client renders the same shell, adopts its existing root and canvases, sizes\ntheir backing stores for the device-pixel ratio, paints the scene, and attaches\nthe shared interaction host. The first image appears after client mount; use\nthe default SVG adapter when visible server-rendered geometry is required.\n\nWhen selected marks use `canvasChartRenderer`, verified server adapters emit\none accessible mixed root with ordered SVG markup and Canvas shells. The\nbrowser adopts each child surface. SVG marks remain visible in the server\nresponse, while Canvas marks receive pixels after mount.\n\n## Fonts and text measurement\n\nAutomatic guide margins depend on text metrics. The server uses deterministic\nfallback measurement unless you provide `measureText`. The browser host\nremeasures when fonts become available and schedules a new layout.\n\n`ChartTextMeasurer` is deliberately synchronous. Its options include the\nresolved family, style, stretch, letter spacing, direction, locale, and font\nscale so server and native implementations can use the same typography\ncontract. Hosts own asynchronous font readiness and request another render\nafter their available metrics change.\n\nFor strict pixel parity:\n\n1. Use a font available in both environments.\n2. Supply a deterministic `ChartTextMeasurer`.\n3. Supply the same `ChartTextTypography`, including locale and font scale, in\n   both environments.\n\nMost applications should allow the browser's post-font layout correction\ninstead of shipping a font engine to the server.\n\n## Render without a framework\n\n`createChartRuntime` and `renderChartSvg` form the server boundary:\n\n```ts\nimport { createChartRuntime, renderChartSvg } from '@tanstack/charts'\n\nconst runtime = createChartRuntime<TrafficRow, Date, number>()\nconst scene = runtime.render(definition, { width: 720, height: 400 })\n\nconst svg = renderChartSvg(scene, {\n  ariaLabel: 'Daily traffic',\n  idPrefix: 'traffic',\n})\n\nruntime.destroy()\n```\n\n`renderChartSvg` returns a string and does not require a DOM. A custom\n`ChartRenderer.prerender` may produce another deterministic shell. Browser-only\nfocus, tooltip, reconciliation or paint, animation, and export begin when its\nsurface mounts.\n\n## Hydration checklist\n\n- Server data is fully resolved before chart rendering.\n- Initial dimensions are explicit and representative.\n- Definition, transformed data, and formatting are deterministic.\n- Keys and `idPrefix` are stable.\n- The same adapter and definition render on both sides.\n- Browser-only work lives in host callbacks or application effects.\n- Font-driven relayout is expected or a text measurer is supplied.\n\nSee the selected framework adapter page and\n[Runtime and Scene](../reference/runtime-and-scene.md) for the exact contracts.\n"}
